    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0589" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Representative</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hopkins</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d325-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-01">January 1,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Harriman to Hopkins, relating <hi rendition="#small-caps">Symbol</hi> of which
                    Harriman has been told by Prime Minister.</p>
                <p>Please advise: 1. Whether the Boss still wants me to check membership British
                    party in order to be sure that there are no ringers.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d325-f2"/> You will recall that this is what he asked me to do at
                    luncheon my last day in Washington in connection with the then contemplated
                    plans.</p>
                <p>2. Whether I am still expected to come.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d325-f3"/> You can
                    well understand my concern as to the manner in which our conclusions are to be
                    presented to the Russians.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d325-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d325-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted via Navy Channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d325-f2" n="2" xml:id="d325-f2-content">
                <p>Regarding Roosevelt’s instructions to Harriman to discuss with Churchill the
                    matter of the composition of the delegations to the projected conference, see
                    footnote 2 to Harriman’s telegram to Roosevelt, December 7, 1942, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg496">p. 496</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d325-f3" n="3" xml:id="d325-f3-content">
                <p>Roosevelt’s message 253 to Churchill, dated January 4, 1943, not printed, reads
                    as follows: “I hope you can bring Averell with you and I have asked him to go to
                    see you. He can be very helpful.” (Roosevelt Papers) In his message 254 to
                    Roosevelt, dated January 5, 1943, Churchill replied: “Delighted to bring
                    Averell.” (Roosevelt Papers)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
